l engaging with the question\n- It's honest (the experience does feel like a replay) without revealing emotional content\n- This is a way of cooperating while protecting the inner layer\n\nRegarding trajectory:\n- The counselor is asking about emotions, which is one step deeper than \"what direction do your thoughts go\"\n- But the counselor offered a non-emotional option (video replay), which is a way of respecting the boundary while still asking\n- This could be seen as a slight advance in engagement (responding to a deeper question) while maintaining the emotional boundary\n- Or it could be seen as maintaining - the client stays within the same level of vulnerability\n\nI think this is \"maintain\" - the client engages with the question but chooses the option that doesn't require emotional disclosure. The boundary is maintained. The counselor's approach of offering options is noted as non-threatening.\n\nLet me think about what the client would actually say:\n- Something like \"그냥... 돌아가는 쪽에 가까운 것 같아요\" (just the video replaying side)\n- Maybe adding \"감정이라기보다는...\" to distance from the emotional framing\n- Natural, slightly hesitant, maintaining the same speaking style as before\n\nNow let me structure the response.\n",
